hadiths[7]{hadithnumber,text}:
"162","Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Mahri narrated to us, Ibn Wahb informed us, Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub informed me, from Yunus ibn Yazid, from Ibn Shihab, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded Hakim ibn Hizam to trade in cloth and food, and forbade him from trading in slaves."
"163","Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Khalid, from Abu Sinan, from 'Abdullah al-Muktib - and he is 'Abdullah ibn al-Harith - he said: A camel was led past the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) being with the people. One of the people said: For how much did you take it? He said: For such-and-such. He added to the price. When he returned home he said: I lied to people among whom was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and told him of the addition. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give the excess in charity."
"164","Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Khalid, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Deceit, trickery, and treachery are in the Fire."
"165","Muhammad ibn al-'Ala' narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr ibn 'Alqamah, from Ibn Abi Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The owner of the goods is most entitled to seek a price."
"166","Abu Tawbah narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed a Bedouin selling something and said: Keep to the first offer and the first market, or the first offer; for profits lie with leniency."
"167","Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from Abu Ya'qub al-Thaqafi, from Khalid - meaning Ibn Abi Malik - he said: I sold goods to Muhammad ibn Sa'd and he said: Give me your hand so I may clasp it, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Blessing lies in hand-clasping."
"168","Muhammad ibn Sulayman al-Anbari narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, from Mujahid, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bought a foal from a Bedouin for one hundred sa' of dates. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a man among them: Go and tell them to measure until they receive in full - meaning the measure. The man went out rubbing with his elbows, meaning he hurried."
